Step 1: Create Empty Web Project
     1. Open Visual Studio 2026.
     2. Click Create a new project.
     3. Select ASP.NET Core Web App (Model-View-Controller).
     4. Click Next.
Step 2: Configure Project
     •   Project Name: BasicPWA
     •   Framework: .NET 10 or latest available on your machine
     •   Click Create.
Step 3: Enable Static Files
Open Program.cs.
Replace the code with:
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
var app = builder.Build();
app.UseDefaultFiles();
app.UseStaticFiles();
app.Run();
Step 4: Create Starting HTML Page
      1. Right-click wwwroot.
      2. Select Add → New Item → HTML Page.
      3. Name the file index.html.
Step 5: Add the Following HTML Code
Write the following code in index.html:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
     <title>Basic PWA</title>
     <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
     <link rel="manifest" href="manifest.json">
</head>
<body>
     <h1>My Progressive Web Application</h1>
     <p>This is the starting page of PWA.</p>
</body>
</html>
Note: Don't miss the following important line.
<link rel="manifest" href="manifest.json">
This connects the HTML page with manifest.json.
Step 6: Create Icons Folder
      1. Right-click wwwroot.
      2. Select Add → New Folder.
         3. Name the folder icons.
         4. Add any two small, downloaded icon files:
                 o   icon1.png
                 o   icon2.png
Place both files inside the icons folder.
Step 7: Create Manifest File
         1. In Solution Explorer, right-click wwwroot.
         2. Select Add → New Item → JSON File.
         3. Name the file manifest.json.
         4. Add the following code to manifest.json.
{
    "name": "Basic Progressive Web Application",
    "short_name": "BasicPWA",
    "description": "Simple PWA Example",
    "start_url": "/index.html",
    "display": "standalone",
    "background_color": "#ffffff",
    "theme_color": "#0d6efd",
    "orientation": "portrait",
    "icons": [
     {
         "src": "/icons/icon1.png",
         "sizes": "192x192",
         "type": "image/png"
        },
        {
            "src": "/icons/icon2.png",
            "sizes": "512x512",
            "type": "image/png"
        }
    ]
}
Step 8: Run Application
Run the application.
The browser opens at an address similar to:
https://localhost:7262/
